[h2][b]Installation[/b][/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]Steam Workshop[/b]: [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3669797690]Notification Filter[/url]
[*] [b]Nexus Mods[/b]: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/x4foundations/mods/1985]Notification Filter[/url]
[/list]
[h2][b]Usage[/b][/h2]

After installation, please open the [b]Extension Option[/b] menu.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-NotificationFilter/refs/heads/main/docs/images/extension_options.png[/img]

[h2]Notification Filter Menu[/h2]

Then, select the [b]Notification Filter[/b] item to open the filter menu.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-NotificationFilter/refs/heads/main/docs/images/notification_filter.png[/img]

The menu contains the following sections:
[list]
[*] Relation Minimum Changes
[*] Money Minimum Changes
[*] Crafting Progress
[*] Collected Items
[*] Station Insufficient Funds
[*] Ship Constructed
[/list]
[h2]Relation Minimum Changes[/h2]

There are two different [b]Dropdowns[/b] to define the minimum change of [b]Relation[/b] to be displayed in [b]Notification ticker[/b] or recorder into `Logbook`:
[list]
[*] `0 - pass all changes`: Equal to the [b]vanilla[/b] game.
[*] `1 point or more`: Only changes of [b]Relation[/b] equal or higher than 1 point will be visible.
[*] `2 points or more`: Only changes of [b]Relation[/b] equal or higher than 2 points will be visible.
[*] `5 points or more`: Only changes of [b]Relation[/b] equal or higher than 5 points will be visible.
[*] `10 points or more`: Only changes of [b]Relation[/b] equal or higher than 10 points will be visible.
[/list]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-NotificationFilter/refs/heads/main/docs/images/notification_filter_relation_dropdown.png[/img]

[h2]Money Minimum Changes[/h2]

There is a [b]Slider[/b] to define the minimum amount of [b]Money[/b] transaction to be displayed in `Notification ticker`.

Acceptable values are between [b]0[/b] and [b]100,000,000[/b] credits with [b]1000[/b] credits step.
Zero value means that all transactions will be visible as in the [b]vanilla[/b] game.

[h2]Crafting Progress[/h2]

There is a [b]Checkbox[/b] to disable notifications related to [b]Crafting Progress[/b] in the [b]Notification ticker[/b] and `Logbook`.

There is an example of such notification in the image below:
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-NotificationFilter/refs/heads/main/docs/images/crafting_progress.png[/img]

[h2]Collected Items[/h2]

There are six [b]Checkboxes[/b] to individually disable notifications for items picked up by the player in the `Notification Ticker`:
[list]
[*] [b]Ammo collected[/b]: Suppresses the [b]Ammo collected[/b] ticker notification.
[*] [b]Ammo received[/b]: Suppresses the [b]Ammo received[/b] (crafted/granted) ticker notification.
[*] [b]Inventory items collected[/b]: Suppresses the [b]Inventory item collected[/b] ticker notification.
[*] [b]Dropped container collected[/b]: Suppresses the [b]Dropped container collected[/b] ticker notification.
[*] [b]Materials collected[/b]: Suppresses the [b]Materials collected[/b] ticker notification.
[*] [b]Storage: 100% full[/b]: Suppresses the [b]Storage: 100% full[/b] (cargo full) ticker notification.
[/list]
[h2]Station Insufficient Funds[/h2]

There are two [b]Checkboxes[/b] to disable notifications related to [b]Station Insufficient Funds[/b] in the [b]Notification ticker[/b] and `Logbook`.

[h2]Ship Constructed[/h2]

There are several [b]Checkboxes[/b] to disable notifications related to [b]Ship Constructed[/b] in the [b]Logbook[/b] based on the size of the constructed ship and [b]Slider[/b] to set a minimum cost of the constructed ship to be recorded in the `Logbook`.

Please take in consideration that:
[list]
[*] These filters are applied only to logbook entries.
[*] The cost filter is applied to all ship sizes, so if the cost of the constructed ship is less than the defined value, the logbook entry will be hidden regardless of the ship size.
[/list]
[h2]Other[/h2]

There is also a [b]Debug[/b] checkbox to enable debug messages for the notifications that are being processed by the filter.

